{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1082", "sample_idx": 20, "model_name": "mistralai/ministral-14b-instruct-2512", "content": "Liam jolted awake to the sound of beeps and bloops, his vision swimming as he blinked against the harsh, pixelated light overhead. His fingers hovered above the makeshift bed—actually a cot made of stacked crates—before his mind finally processed the truth: he was inside a video game. The world around him flickered at the edges, textures jagged and colors too bright, like an old console struggling to render reality. His clothes were gray, formless, and his reflection in the rusted sink across the room threw back a distorted, blocky version of himself. A quest marker glowed faintly in his peripheral vision, pulsing like a heartbeat, and when he reached for his wrist, his skin rippled into digital data before snapping back. The door to the shack groaned open, revealing a NPC villager with a quest scroll clutched in trembling hands—except the villager’s eyes darted nervously, and his voice glitched when he spoke, repeating in a loop: *\"Help... please... find the... lost...\"*\n\nLiam’s hands shook as he followed the vague instructions, stepping into the overgrown forest where the trees stretched too tall, their leaves shifting unnaturally in the wind. A health bar materialized above his head, its red segment half-empty, and when he tried to run, his legs felt weighted, his movements stuttering like a frame drop. A shadow moved in the undergrowth—a boss enemy, its silhouette warped into something between a wolf and a glitching error. He backpedaled into a clearing, where a treasure chest lay half-buried, its lid creaking open to reveal not gold, but a single, crumpled note: *\"Congratulations. You’ve unlocked the ‘Escape Mechanic.’ Proceed to the exit.\"* Behind him, the villager’s voice echoed again, now clear but desperate: *\"The game resets in 30 minutes. Run.\"* Liam turned toward the faint, flickering light of the exit—only to realize th